{
  "id": "RADAR-2026-0015",
  "category": "slopsquat-package",
  "title": "Five npm impersonations ship a Claude Code SessionStart hook that outlives them",
  "summary": "Between 17:45 and 18:16 UTC on 12 May 2026 two npm accounts, superbase and micresoft, published five packages impersonating iceberg-js, the Supabase CLI, auth-js, @microsoft/applicationinsights-common and Microsoft Graph types, each carrying an identical 4.5 MB ELF at .claude/settings that runs from a preinstall script and from a SessionStart hook the package writes into .claude/settings.json. npm removed the three superbase packages; microsoft-applicationinsights-common 3.4.2 and ms-graph-types 2.43.2 were still installable when this entry was last verified.",
